Syntax: strip <item>

Strip cuts a piece of armor down a tier: heavy becomes medium, medium light,
light clothing.  The classes locked out of it by that tier can wear it once
you are done, and the armor it offers falls to match.

The item's own level is what falls, rescaled by the ratio between the two
tiers, so a fine piece stripped down is still a fine piece of what it now
is.  Nothing is capped and nothing is gained: stripping only ever takes
away, which is why it answers to no skill ceiling.

The work is measured by the item's structure and a clumsy cut costs it a
point of that.  Intelligence is what keeps your knife off the piece; wits
enough and a slip costs only the time.  An item cut to nothing is destroyed.

Light armor stripped to clothing stops being armor at all and becomes a
worn thing, which is a different sort of object entirely.

See also: PLATE, BANGLE, BOLSTER
